#: includes/wp/class-aitp-admin-audit.php:240
msgid "Off by default. Works through \"wrong\" findings of page text one batch at a time: backs up and resets one batch, visits only the pages that show those strings until they are translated again, checks the new translations, and starts the next batch only when the batch came out clean. It stops by itself when more than 5% of a batch is still wrong or untranslated, when English is stored as a translation, on provider errors or failed page loads, when TranslatePress no longer uses this engine, or when a batch is rolled back. \"Probably misplaced\" and \"check meaning\" findings, the accepted list, manual translations, structured data and interface text are never touched. Every batch can be rolled back under \"Repairs\". Try a few batches by hand first."
msgstr ""

